1
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:18,560
Sir! Over here!

2
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:24,065
<i>The sleeve.</i>

3
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:29,070
<i>The scorched sleeve.</i>

4
00:00:35,785 --> 00:00:37,370
<i>Why am I only remembering this now?</i>

5
00:00:41,499 --> 00:00:44,419
NO CALLER ID

6
00:00:45,628 --> 00:00:46,963
<i>Did you get the ticket?</i>

7
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:49,507
<i>The flight's tomorrow.</i>

8
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:51,634
You know why it's Jeju, right?

9
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:53,803
Yes.

10
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:56,473
I'll see you there.

11
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:18,703
<i>It was the same ship back then.</i>

12
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:20,538
<i>Do you remember?</i>

13
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:21,998
<i>Je Moon-jae?</i>

14
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:28,022
<i>Hello, this is Sky Sunset Vacation Home.</i>

15
00:02:28,106 --> 00:02:30,233
Hello. I'd like to confirm my reservation.

16
00:02:30,775 --> 00:02:31,985
It's under Je Moon-jae.

17
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:33,736
Yes, for two.

18
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:36,656
Okay. I'll see you when I check in.

19
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:16,070
<i>I'll disappear just like that.</i>

20
00:03:16,654 --> 00:03:18,531
<i>In the end, you'll be the only one left.</i>

21
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:21,326
<i>That's how our story ends.</i>

22
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:20,176
MOUSETRAP

23
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:22,470
Easy. It stings.

24
00:04:23,471 --> 00:04:24,389
It stings.

25
00:04:24,472 --> 00:04:26,057
Sir!

26
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:28,518
- It really hurts!
- Quit whining, you bastard.

27
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,396
- Gently.
- Dong-cheol, maybe it's broken.

28
00:04:31,896 --> 00:04:33,523
Hey! I said it really hurts.

29
00:04:33,606 --> 00:04:34,440
Goddamn.

30
00:04:34,524 --> 00:04:36,276
- Think I'm kidding?
- He's awake.

31
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:37,694
Oh.

32
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:39,612
- Oh man.
- Hey.

33
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:41,114
Just stay down, you punk.

34
00:04:41,781 --> 00:04:42,782
What about the uncle?

35
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:44,450
Couldn't find him.

36
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:47,578
We couldn't find him,
but we did find a witness.

37
00:04:48,871 --> 00:04:50,164
A railway crew member.

38
00:04:50,248 --> 00:04:52,417
<i>He asked</i>
<i>how to get to Children's Grand Park,</i>

39
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:54,210
<i>like he had somewhere to be.</i>

40
00:04:55,044 --> 00:04:57,005
<i>He said he had to go find someone.</i>

41
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:01,759
What about Noja and that bastard?

42
00:05:01,843 --> 00:05:03,052
We lost them.

43
00:05:03,678 --> 00:05:05,263
Major Crimes will find them.

44
00:05:11,185 --> 00:05:12,020
Hey.

45
00:05:12,103 --> 00:05:13,646
- Hey!
- What are you…

46
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:15,690
Hey, you've lost a lot of blood.

47
00:05:15,773 --> 00:05:17,400
- Stick it in quickly.
- I'm fine.

48
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:18,943
Hey.

49
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:19,861
You two.

50
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:22,238
Track down writer Je Moon-jae now.

51
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:24,324
Those two will definitely show up there.

52
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:27,618
Kid, you're coming with me.
Let's go somewhere.

53
00:05:28,619 --> 00:05:30,955
- Hey, do you have an extra T-shirt?
- I do.

54
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:31,956
Captain, sir.

55
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:36,294
What should I do, sir?

56
00:05:36,377 --> 00:05:37,503
You

57
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:39,881
just go home, wash up, and get some rest.

58
00:05:40,381 --> 00:05:42,342
Hui-jeong's a senior in high school.

59
00:05:46,512 --> 00:05:48,806
She started university last year,
you damn bastard.

60
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:51,559
You didn't even know that?

61
00:05:53,394 --> 00:05:54,228
Let's go.

62
00:06:26,803 --> 00:06:27,887
Yes?

63
00:06:44,529 --> 00:06:45,863
It's been a while,

64
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:47,407
Yu-min.

65
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:11,722
Hey, it's me.

66
00:07:11,806 --> 00:07:14,267
Get a car to the airport.
Four in the morning tomorrow.

67
00:07:15,351 --> 00:07:17,437
Shit, I don't know how long I'll be there.

68
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:19,147
See you when I get there.

69
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:20,481
Yeah.

70
00:07:25,069 --> 00:07:26,320
Fuck.

71
00:08:17,079 --> 00:08:18,623
Are you an American?

72
00:08:19,123 --> 00:08:21,918
Why the fuck are you coming in
with your fucking shoes on?

73
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:32,803
Oh, come on!

74
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:34,388
Let's not do this.

75
00:08:34,472 --> 00:08:37,808
You've got a new life now.
Try to be a better person.

76
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:40,102
I'll be a new person too. Okay?

77
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:02,500
He said he was going to find someone?

78
00:09:04,043 --> 00:09:06,003
Like he had somewhere to be?

79
00:09:07,046 --> 00:09:08,506
It's okay. Don't cry.

80
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:11,217
Who did this?

81
00:09:21,602 --> 00:09:22,645
Moon-jae.

82
00:09:24,730 --> 00:09:25,982
<i>Moon-jae!</i>

83
00:09:26,065 --> 00:09:26,983
He's here?

84
00:09:28,109 --> 00:09:28,985
The uncle?

85
00:09:30,069 --> 00:09:31,404
I have a feeling

86
00:09:33,114 --> 00:09:35,741
his memory might be stuck here.

87
00:09:37,785 --> 00:09:38,995
You stay here.

88
00:09:50,172 --> 00:09:52,508
You've buried a lot of people too.

89
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:54,176
Fuck.

90
00:09:54,677 --> 00:09:57,680
You can do it, but I can't?

91
00:10:04,478 --> 00:10:05,563
Let's

92
00:10:06,063 --> 00:10:07,940
stay alive together.

93
00:10:08,024 --> 00:10:09,734
Once I get my money back…

94
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:12,069
Fucking hell.

95
00:10:12,653 --> 00:10:14,488
Let the living live.

96
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:17,199
Shut up, you son of a bitch.

97
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:26,000
That bastard Dong-seok begged for his life

98
00:10:26,083 --> 00:10:28,294
the same way you are now,
you son of a bitch.

99
00:10:28,377 --> 00:10:31,130
I told him to keep it under control
and not cross the line.

100
00:10:31,213 --> 00:10:33,341
He got killed for stealing from the gang.

101
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:35,176
He wanted to start a new life.

102
00:10:35,259 --> 00:10:38,012
You dipped into the gang's money too.

103
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:39,472
Yeah.

104
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:43,851
I wanted to start a new life too.
You fucking bastard!

105
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:48,230
I'm so sick of this shit,
you son of a bitch!

106
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:53,861
Stay alive together?
Let's say I let you live.

107
00:10:54,528 --> 00:10:57,198
Are you gonna leave me alone?

108
00:10:59,408 --> 00:11:00,743
I promise you, Noja.

109
00:11:01,661 --> 00:11:02,745
Fuck.

110
00:11:02,828 --> 00:11:05,456
You'll never ever see me again.

111
00:11:05,539 --> 00:11:07,416
Can I trust you on that?

112
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:08,334
Never…

113
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:10,961
Never ever…

114
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:36,654
Never what? Fucking bastard.

115
00:11:36,737 --> 00:11:39,740
Never what?
Never go back to living like trash?

116
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:42,159
Since when were we human?

117
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:44,036
Then get yourself a new identity.

118
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:46,080
You fucking dumbass!

119
00:11:46,163 --> 00:11:46,997
Got it?

120
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:54,004
How can people like us live
without creating new characters?

121
00:11:55,005 --> 00:11:56,757
When you buried Dong-seok, shit,

122
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:58,884
you were cold as fuck.

123
00:11:59,385 --> 00:12:00,803
Fucking bastard.

124
00:12:00,886 --> 00:12:02,388
If you hesitate,

125
00:12:02,471 --> 00:12:05,683
you fucking die, you dumbass!

126
00:12:11,897 --> 00:12:13,190
Fuck.

127
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:25,244
I have to get another one. Fuck.

128
00:12:30,249 --> 00:12:33,836
Min-yeong, you, and I used this room
last time we were on board, right?

129
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:38,299
The ship's horn during our call.
I knew you were gonna get on this ship.

130
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:43,262
But we didn't agree to meet here.

131
00:12:43,345 --> 00:12:46,515
But who knows what kind of trap
you've set there?

132
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:57,026
Tell me why you did all this shit.

133
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:02,114
Tell me!

134
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:06,702
You really don't know why?

135
00:13:11,957 --> 00:13:13,375
I don't know!

136
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:16,003
I don't know, you bastard!

137
00:13:18,547 --> 00:13:22,468
No matter how much I think about it,
I don't know, you bastard!

138
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:30,643
I don't know, you bastard.

139
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:42,738
What reason could there be?

140
00:13:44,365 --> 00:13:45,574
I just want to be you.

141
00:13:49,328 --> 00:13:50,663
That place

142
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:52,998
was never yours to begin with.

143
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:56,377
You're not even Je Moon-jae.

144
00:13:58,337 --> 00:13:59,296
Huh?

145
00:14:06,345 --> 00:14:08,013
<i>Moon-jae, where are you?</i>

146
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:10,349
Moon-jae!

147
00:14:11,141 --> 00:14:12,518
<i>Moon-jae!</i>

148
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:22,361
<i>Moon-jae!</i>

149
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:25,489
Moon-jae!

150
00:14:58,272 --> 00:14:59,273
<i>You didn't know?</i>

151
00:15:01,525 --> 00:15:03,235
That the detective was your brother?

152
00:15:07,781 --> 00:15:10,701
I guess you two didn't talk about that
when he interrogated you.

153
00:15:11,201 --> 00:15:14,622
I thought he smuggled you out
because you two were brothers.

154
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,504
Before you were born,

155
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:25,716
he was the real Je Moon-jae.

156
00:15:26,216 --> 00:15:27,051
That detective.

157
00:15:34,308 --> 00:15:35,809
What's this?

158
00:15:41,774 --> 00:15:43,692
You were a fake from birth.

159
00:15:45,235 --> 00:15:47,112
When you were born, he was sent away.

160
00:15:49,281 --> 00:15:50,491
You took his place.

161
00:15:51,992 --> 00:15:54,411
I brought him in to catch you.

162
00:15:54,495 --> 00:15:58,874
But the damn uncle suddenly showed up.
So things got a bit messed up.

163
00:16:02,461 --> 00:16:03,629
Why am I doing this?

164
00:16:12,554 --> 00:16:14,890
Because you took everything from me.

165
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:18,268
Me?

166
00:16:19,311 --> 00:16:20,270
Yes.

167
00:16:21,814 --> 00:16:23,107
Even Min-yeong.

168
00:16:25,192 --> 00:16:26,068
Huh?

169
00:16:29,863 --> 00:16:32,282
Did you guys see the post?
That's So Min-yeong.

170
00:16:32,366 --> 00:16:34,451
- You're right.
- It's her, right?

171
00:16:35,077 --> 00:16:37,037
She's got some nerve showing up here.

172
00:16:37,121 --> 00:16:38,789
If I were her, I couldn't.

173
00:16:38,872 --> 00:16:39,915
Isn't that Seo Yu-min?

174
00:16:39,999 --> 00:16:41,959
What? Are they still seeing each other?

175
00:16:42,042 --> 00:16:43,419
<i>You have a knack for it.</i>

176
00:16:44,545 --> 00:16:46,714
<i>Mixing truth with lies.</i>

177
00:16:47,506 --> 00:16:49,174
ANONYMOUS FORUM
LOATHSOME RATS 1

178
00:16:49,258 --> 00:16:51,427
THE SOUND OF THEIR BREATHING
COMING FROM THEIR ROOM…

179
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:53,512
<i>With all the rumors going around school,</i>

180
00:16:53,595 --> 00:16:55,639
<i>Min-yeong had to give up on grad school.</i>

181
00:16:59,768 --> 00:17:03,814
<i>You must've been one hell of a writer.</i>
<i>Even the cops had nothing on you.</i>

182
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:07,151
The person who wrote that dirty post
is Moon-jae.

183
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:10,362
<i>I wanted to beat you to death,</i>
<i>but I had no idea where you were.</i>

184
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:13,073
Everybody knows it's about us!

185
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:17,953
<i>After that, Min-yeong dropped out</i>
<i>and cut ties with her family.</i>

186
00:17:19,788 --> 00:17:22,875
<i>She became a wreck</i>
<i>who couldn't sleep without sleeping pills.</i>

187
00:17:25,044 --> 00:17:27,546
<i>Then she tried to kill herself</i>
<i>with sleeping pills.</i>

188
00:17:29,631 --> 00:17:30,966
<i>There was nothing I could do.</i>

189
00:17:32,259 --> 00:17:33,886
<i>I didn't even have any money.</i>

190
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:37,848
<i>But I had to save her. She was dying.</i>

191
00:17:46,273 --> 00:17:49,568
<i>So I took my writing to a publisher,</i>
<i>hoping to sell it, and found out.</i>

192
00:17:55,949 --> 00:17:57,409
INTERVIEW
BY SUNG HAG-YUN

193
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:03,999
<i>My novel had already been published</i>
<i>and won the Best New Writer award.</i>

194
00:18:04,083 --> 00:18:05,084
INTERVIEW

195
00:18:09,671 --> 00:18:13,050
<i>You took my life, my future,</i>

196
00:18:13,801 --> 00:18:15,886
<i>everything from me.</i>

197
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:19,932
<i>Even Min-yeong.</i>

198
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:35,072
I wanted to tell her so badly.

199
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:39,034
I wanted to tell her
I'd finally found that bastard.

200
00:18:41,036 --> 00:18:43,288
<i>But there's no one left to listen.</i>

201
00:18:57,219 --> 00:18:59,680
Min-yeong.

202
00:19:01,849 --> 00:19:02,850
Min-yeong.

203
00:19:06,061 --> 00:19:07,229
Min-yeong.

204
00:19:08,272 --> 00:19:09,314
Min-yeong.

205
00:19:10,732 --> 00:19:11,567
Min-yeong.

206
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:15,195
Min-yeong.

207
00:19:20,367 --> 00:19:23,412
<i>I stayed by Min-yeong's side all night,</i>
<i>thinking of only one thing.</i>

208
00:19:25,497 --> 00:19:27,166
<i>"How should I pay this back?"</i>

209
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:37,384
<i>Night after night, I read your novels</i>
<i>beside Min-yeong's body.</i>

210
00:19:37,885 --> 00:19:39,094
<i>From beginning to end.</i>

211
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:41,930
<i>Without missing a single word.</i>

212
00:19:44,516 --> 00:19:45,851
You took everything.

213
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:50,147
You became me,
and Min-yeong became your girlfriend.

214
00:19:50,647 --> 00:19:54,610
<i>You were so jealous of me that,</i>
<i>in your novel,</i>

215
00:19:55,402 --> 00:19:58,030
you subtly made yourself me and me you.

216
00:19:59,239 --> 00:20:01,491
So I decided.

217
00:20:04,745 --> 00:20:06,079
I'll get my revenge.

218
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:09,041
I'll become you too

219
00:20:09,541 --> 00:20:12,044
and take back everything you took from me.

220
00:20:13,837 --> 00:20:16,173
I'll rip that mask off your face,

221
00:20:16,256 --> 00:20:18,383
strip you of everything,
and throw you out.

222
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:21,053
Satisfied now?

223
00:20:21,553 --> 00:20:25,474
Does that answer your question?
Why I became a monster?

224
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:30,520
Welcome.

225
00:20:42,866 --> 00:20:47,788
An antiseptic, bandages,
a hemostatic agent, and painkillers.

226
00:20:47,871 --> 00:20:48,789
Hang on.

227
00:20:48,872 --> 00:20:52,334
Sir, shouldn't you go to the hospital?

228
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:56,088
I'll

229
00:20:57,172 --> 00:20:58,507
handle it myself.

230
00:21:03,637 --> 00:21:04,680
Moon-jae

231
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:07,057
went to meet the rat bastard.

232
00:21:07,641 --> 00:21:09,101
The one who looks just like him.

233
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:13,438
That bastard doesn't even know who he is.

234
00:21:14,022 --> 00:21:15,857
No matter who he used to be…

235
00:21:18,485 --> 00:21:20,028
he really is Je Moon-jae.

236
00:21:21,446 --> 00:21:22,698
Save him.

237
00:21:23,532 --> 00:21:25,325
I don't think I can go there.

238
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:28,578
<i>He might fall into a trap and die.</i>

239
00:21:28,662 --> 00:21:30,789
<i>You go save him.</i>

240
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,374
<i>Catch him,</i>

241
00:21:32,874 --> 00:21:36,545
and if he's guilty,
throw him in prison or whatever.

242
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:38,797
Save him

243
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:41,174
for now.

244
00:21:44,136 --> 00:21:45,053
Please.

245
00:21:51,059 --> 00:21:51,977
Unbelievable.

246
00:21:52,686 --> 00:21:54,980
He still trusts that bastard?

247
00:21:57,691 --> 00:22:00,235
Fine, fuck it. I'll check it out.

248
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:04,031
Hey, have you figured out
where writer Je Moon-jae is?

249
00:22:04,531 --> 00:22:05,365
Yes.

250
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:06,575
Where is he?

251
00:22:06,658 --> 00:22:07,617
He's at sea.

252
00:22:16,293 --> 00:22:17,377
I

253
00:22:18,628 --> 00:22:19,921
just wrote that.

254
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:21,214
I was high on drugs.

255
00:22:21,298 --> 00:22:25,052
Hey, who'd read that bullshit?
I just wrote it like a novel.

256
00:22:26,428 --> 00:22:28,555
That's why Min-yeong killed herself?

257
00:22:34,102 --> 00:22:35,729
What about the woman you killed?

258
00:22:35,812 --> 00:22:36,897
Someone else.

259
00:22:38,231 --> 00:22:40,609
<i>You know that thug?</i>
<i>The one who does identity fraud?</i>

260
00:22:41,443 --> 00:22:43,278
<i>I used him a bit.</i>

261
00:22:48,367 --> 00:22:49,242
Why?

262
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:52,704
To frame me?

263
00:22:53,830 --> 00:22:54,664
Yeah.

264
00:22:56,416 --> 00:22:58,502
You crazy bastard. You fucking nutjob!

265
00:22:58,585 --> 00:23:01,797
You're the bastard who posed
as a university student with a fake ID!

266
00:23:04,424 --> 00:23:07,052
Are you crazy
or just pretending to be crazy?

267
00:23:12,641 --> 00:23:13,892
Hold on.

268
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:17,145
You bastard.

269
00:23:17,854 --> 00:23:19,689
You're not lying.

270
00:23:21,233 --> 00:23:23,110
You're not hiding behind lame excuses

271
00:23:23,193 --> 00:23:26,113
like panic disorder and depression
after stealing someone's life.

272
00:23:29,783 --> 00:23:31,118
Hey, are you crazy?

273
00:23:31,701 --> 00:23:32,577
Are you insane?

274
00:23:33,412 --> 00:23:35,372
Get a grip, man.

275
00:23:35,455 --> 00:23:36,456
You…

276
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:39,292
You're the bad guy, you bastard!

277
00:23:41,378 --> 00:23:43,338
You don't remember stealing my notebooks?

278
00:23:44,214 --> 00:23:46,550
Everything in your novels
came from my notebooks.

279
00:23:46,633 --> 00:23:49,261
You're the fake university student,
you bastard!

280
00:23:50,303 --> 00:23:51,138
Those were

281
00:23:51,805 --> 00:23:53,014
my notebooks…

282
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:54,349
What is it?

283
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:57,060
Why are you trailing off? Huh?

284
00:23:57,144 --> 00:23:58,270
You're not so confident?

285
00:24:00,564 --> 00:24:02,899
Min-yeong was my junior in the department.

286
00:24:05,777 --> 00:24:07,195
She went out with me.

287
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:09,781
That's all from your novel,
you crazy bastard!

288
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:12,576
That's not reality, you bastard!

289
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:17,289
Why?

290
00:24:17,789 --> 00:24:19,207
Why do you want to be me?

291
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:21,042
Huh?

292
00:24:26,798 --> 00:24:28,175
<i>Now I remember.</i>

293
00:24:38,894 --> 00:24:41,438
<i>Now I understand</i>
<i>why I couldn't write anything</i>

294
00:24:42,189 --> 00:24:43,565
<i>for some time now.</i>

295
00:24:44,858 --> 00:24:46,318
<i>None of it</i>

296
00:24:46,985 --> 00:24:49,321
<i>was ever mine to begin with.</i>

297
00:24:58,872 --> 00:25:00,999
<i>After barely overcoming my panic disorder,</i>

298
00:25:01,583 --> 00:25:03,835
<i>I wanted to become</i>
<i>a better version of myself,</i>

299
00:25:04,628 --> 00:25:07,547
<i>like my mom always told me.</i>

300
00:25:08,048 --> 00:25:10,717
INTERCOLLEGIATE LITERATURE CLUB
RECRUITING NEW MEMBERS

301
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:12,010
Hey, guys. Listen up.

302
00:25:13,011 --> 00:25:14,638
We got a new member today.

303
00:25:14,721 --> 00:25:16,848
Hello, I'm Je Moon-jae.

304
00:25:16,932 --> 00:25:18,642
It's very nice to meet you all.

305
00:25:21,102 --> 00:25:22,145
Have a seat.

306
00:25:50,423 --> 00:25:51,424
You eat first.

307
00:25:54,928 --> 00:25:56,096
- It's good, right?
- Yeah.

308
00:25:57,055 --> 00:25:58,640
I'll eat the burnt part again.

309
00:25:58,723 --> 00:26:00,684
Hey, looking good, you two.

310
00:26:01,351 --> 00:26:02,185
Huh?

311
00:26:03,353 --> 00:26:04,479
Something might happen.

312
00:26:06,856 --> 00:26:08,608
Stop drinking. You're already drunk.

313
00:26:14,322 --> 00:26:15,907
Min-yeong. Let's talk.

314
00:26:16,408 --> 00:26:18,243
- You're drunk. Talk tomorrow.
- Fuck.

315
00:26:18,326 --> 00:26:19,703
Let go, you bastard.

316
00:26:19,786 --> 00:26:20,620
What are you?

317
00:26:20,704 --> 00:26:22,289
You said you two weren't a thing.

318
00:26:23,373 --> 00:26:24,624
We're dating.

319
00:26:24,708 --> 00:26:29,462
We kept it a secret at the club
because it'd be awkward if people knew.

320
00:26:33,133 --> 00:26:34,175
Since when?

321
00:26:35,343 --> 00:26:36,761
Since before you asked me.

322
00:26:39,055 --> 00:26:43,393
Fuck. You two shouldn't toy with people.

323
00:26:43,476 --> 00:26:44,686
Huh?

324
00:27:10,045 --> 00:27:11,880
You are just jealous of me.

325
00:27:12,380 --> 00:27:15,550
You're dying of jealousy
because you want to be me.

326
00:27:17,135 --> 00:27:18,219
Aren't you?

327
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:21,681
Shut up.

328
00:27:21,765 --> 00:27:23,475
I said shut up.

329
00:28:01,054 --> 00:28:01,888
<i>I was</i>

330
00:28:03,181 --> 00:28:04,808
the fake university student?

331
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:09,020
I never dated Min-yeong…

332
00:28:11,272 --> 00:28:13,233
and all my novels were yours?

333
00:28:26,996 --> 00:28:28,707
Were you always crazy?

334
00:28:28,790 --> 00:28:30,834
Or did the meds make you crazy?

335
00:28:31,418 --> 00:28:32,794
Yu-min.

336
00:28:34,337 --> 00:28:35,505
Then was I…

337
00:28:38,591 --> 00:28:40,135
Was I the Rat?

338
00:28:48,435 --> 00:28:50,979
You weren't supposed to show up here.

339
00:28:52,147 --> 00:28:55,900
That beach.
You should've come to that vacation home.

340
00:28:55,984 --> 00:28:58,153
I should've disappeared there forever,

341
00:28:59,279 --> 00:29:02,073
and you should've been exposed
to the world as the real Rat.

342
00:29:02,157 --> 00:29:03,450
That was our ending.

343
00:29:14,169 --> 00:29:15,003
Sir!

344
00:29:16,337 --> 00:29:17,422
Sir!

345
00:29:18,715 --> 00:29:20,216
- Go get the master key.
- Sir.

346
00:29:20,300 --> 00:29:21,134
Sir!

347
00:29:21,217 --> 00:29:22,886
Do you know what's going on?

348
00:29:22,969 --> 00:29:24,429
Open up! Sir! Are you okay?

349
00:29:24,512 --> 00:29:26,306
One of us

350
00:29:28,057 --> 00:29:30,477
has to disappear forever right here.

351
00:29:30,977 --> 00:29:33,646
Before they open the door!

352
00:29:33,730 --> 00:29:34,856
Sir, are you okay?

353
00:29:36,608 --> 00:29:37,442
Sir, open up!

354
00:29:37,525 --> 00:29:39,027
Just die.

355
00:29:41,196 --> 00:29:42,822
I'll live as Je Moon-jae.

356
00:30:34,374 --> 00:30:36,668
Everyone should be out.
Why can't we see him?

357
00:30:36,751 --> 00:30:38,503
You checked the passenger list, right?

358
00:30:38,586 --> 00:30:41,714
I did. I checked
that writer Je Moon-jae was on board.

359
00:30:49,931 --> 00:30:52,475
WRITER JE MOON-JAE

360
00:31:27,802 --> 00:31:28,845
What's going on?

361
00:31:28,928 --> 00:31:30,972
He said there was an accident last night.

362
00:31:31,931 --> 00:31:33,099
What accident?

363
00:31:40,148 --> 00:31:42,317
He snuck on board that ship.

364
00:31:42,817 --> 00:31:44,068
To kill me.

365
00:31:44,152 --> 00:31:45,194
We checked the CCTV.

366
00:31:45,778 --> 00:31:47,697
There was someone who looked like him.

367
00:31:50,408 --> 00:31:51,701
What is he talking about?

368
00:31:51,784 --> 00:31:52,619
And?

369
00:31:54,412 --> 00:31:55,788
He fell into the ocean.

370
00:31:56,539 --> 00:31:59,208
He tried to throw me out the window,
but fell himself.

371
00:32:01,044 --> 00:32:03,296
I think he thought killing me
would make him me.

372
00:32:22,649 --> 00:32:26,069
I'm glad you found my uncle.
We should do the DNA test right away.

373
00:32:27,779 --> 00:32:28,905
In due time.

374
00:32:29,989 --> 00:32:31,741
Not that I think we need to.

375
00:32:32,617 --> 00:32:35,119
I told you, I'm Je Moon-jae.

376
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:38,206
Even if he'd killed me,
he couldn't have proven he was me anyway.

377
00:32:38,289 --> 00:32:40,625
He wouldn't have known
you'd find my uncle.

378
00:32:44,587 --> 00:32:46,547
Thanks to you, I'll clear my name.

379
00:32:48,174 --> 00:32:49,008
The button.

380
00:32:51,010 --> 00:32:53,972
- What?
- Button up your shirt all the way.

381
00:32:56,391 --> 00:32:57,934
That's how he wears it.

382
00:33:14,534 --> 00:33:16,494
Why are you going this far?

383
00:33:22,458 --> 00:33:23,918
I don't follow…

384
00:33:24,711 --> 00:33:27,588
You can drop the act. I'm not recording.

385
00:33:29,674 --> 00:33:31,175
Isn't killing the fake enough?

386
00:33:31,259 --> 00:33:32,260
Why?

387
00:33:32,969 --> 00:33:34,971
Why are you pretending to be the fake one?

388
00:33:36,222 --> 00:33:39,726
Was there something else he had
that you wanted?

389
00:33:45,481 --> 00:33:48,359
You always take someone's place…

390
00:36:09,125 --> 00:36:10,209
Did you really

391
00:36:11,586 --> 00:36:13,296
want to be me that badly?

392
00:36:16,632 --> 00:36:18,634
I don't think I wanted to be you.

393
00:36:20,094 --> 00:36:21,846
I think I wanted to be myself.

394
00:36:23,264 --> 00:36:24,682
A better version of myself.

395
00:36:43,910 --> 00:36:45,161
This isn't the end.

396
00:36:46,662 --> 00:36:48,539
You won't be able to handle it.

397
00:37:50,977 --> 00:37:52,061
Long ago…

398
00:37:54,939 --> 00:37:56,649
my mom told me this all the time.

399
00:37:59,610 --> 00:38:03,072
"You have to be a better Je Moon-jae
than the old Moon-jae."

400
00:38:04,115 --> 00:38:05,366
Now…

401
00:38:07,368 --> 00:38:09,245
I understand what it meant.

402
00:38:12,331 --> 00:38:15,501
I heard you were Je Moon-jae once.

403
00:38:22,633 --> 00:38:24,802
I think there's a misunderstanding here.

404
00:38:24,885 --> 00:38:26,887
That place was always mine.

405
00:38:28,389 --> 00:38:30,433
I didn't take it from you.

406
00:38:40,693 --> 00:38:42,570
Keep that place all to yourself.

407
00:38:43,404 --> 00:38:44,363
Why would I care?

408
00:38:45,072 --> 00:38:47,074
Let's never cross paths again.

409
00:40:02,274 --> 00:40:04,193
Oh, you changed your style.

410
00:40:06,028 --> 00:40:07,113
Looks fucking awful.

411
00:40:14,495 --> 00:40:15,496
Are you hurt badly?

412
00:40:15,579 --> 00:40:17,581
It just grazed me, you punk.

413
00:40:19,708 --> 00:40:20,709
And the hospital?

414
00:40:22,920 --> 00:40:23,754
Did you eat?

415
00:40:42,064 --> 00:40:43,774
You're not popping your meds anymore?

416
00:40:45,526 --> 00:40:47,153
No, not anymore.

417
00:40:47,736 --> 00:40:48,737
I'm all better.

418
00:40:53,242 --> 00:40:54,452
What's with your arm?

419
00:40:56,036 --> 00:40:58,456
I don't fucking know.
It just doesn't move.

420
00:40:58,956 --> 00:41:01,250
Then you should go to the hospital.

421
00:41:01,876 --> 00:41:03,627
Hospital? You bastard.

422
00:41:03,711 --> 00:41:05,796
Want me to turn myself in
over a knife fight?

423
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:08,257
Well, it worked out.

424
00:41:08,340 --> 00:41:10,593
It's a forced retirement.

425
00:41:10,676 --> 00:41:11,927
Right? I'm old too.

426
00:41:13,012 --> 00:41:15,097
The karma I built up with my fists.

427
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:17,266
I'm paying it off with one arm.

428
00:41:17,349 --> 00:41:18,767
Then what are you gonna do now?

429
00:41:21,437 --> 00:41:23,772
You punk, since when do you care about me?

430
00:41:24,940 --> 00:41:25,941
Are we close, punk?

431
00:41:26,859 --> 00:41:28,652
Well, it's partly my fault.

432
00:41:30,529 --> 00:41:32,072
I'm trying to help you now.

433
00:41:32,156 --> 00:41:33,616
Cut the bullshit. Damn it.

434
00:41:35,493 --> 00:41:38,871
I don't need help from a punk like you.

435
00:41:43,250 --> 00:41:44,376
Anyway…

436
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:46,253
So,

437
00:41:47,463 --> 00:41:49,465
are you the fake one or the real one?

438
00:42:04,813 --> 00:42:06,524
That fire on the school trip.

439
00:42:09,944 --> 00:42:11,278
<i>I started that fire.</i>

440
00:42:16,367 --> 00:42:19,578
<i>I remember everything</i>
<i>now that I'm off the meds.</i>

441
00:42:21,747 --> 00:42:23,499
I was the one who started the fire.

442
00:42:24,917 --> 00:42:25,876
Why'd you do it?

443
00:42:27,002 --> 00:42:29,922
Something happened
the day before the school trip.

444
00:42:30,005 --> 00:42:32,758
CHEONGUN CRAM SCHOOL
FOR MIDDLE AND HIGH SCHOOL STUDENTS

445
00:42:32,841 --> 00:42:34,677
Who's Park Chan-u?

446
00:42:37,888 --> 00:42:40,140
Why'd you register under a different name?

447
00:42:43,894 --> 00:42:45,020
Don't like your name?

448
00:42:46,730 --> 00:42:47,565
I don't.

449
00:42:48,315 --> 00:42:49,400
Why?

450
00:42:50,317 --> 00:42:53,779
It doesn't feel like my name.
I don't want to live with it.

451
00:42:53,862 --> 00:42:55,155
How come?

452
00:42:57,157 --> 00:43:01,495
<i>You have to be a better Je Moon-jae</i>
<i>than the old Moon-jae.</i>

453
00:43:03,622 --> 00:43:06,542
Whether at home or at school,

454
00:43:06,625 --> 00:43:08,836
I had nothing to show for it.

455
00:43:08,919 --> 00:43:11,547
You know, nothing special.

456
00:43:12,548 --> 00:43:14,466
I was neither this nor that.

457
00:43:15,050 --> 00:43:18,095
I think that's why my mom and father
didn't like me.

458
00:43:20,222 --> 00:43:21,974
I didn't like myself for it either.

459
00:43:23,142 --> 00:43:26,770
So I guess I wanted to be different
that night.

460
00:43:29,273 --> 00:43:30,858
Like being reborn, I guess?

461
00:43:31,358 --> 00:43:32,443
You know,

462
00:43:32,943 --> 00:43:38,407
a kid who would only cross on green,
even when no cars were coming,

463
00:43:39,408 --> 00:43:43,996
became someone who could cross on red
for the first time that night.

464
00:43:46,749 --> 00:43:48,667
It was like a reset button.

465
00:43:49,168 --> 00:43:50,294
That fire.

466
00:43:50,377 --> 00:43:51,587
So,

467
00:43:52,713 --> 00:43:54,506
did you switch names again?

468
00:43:56,884 --> 00:43:58,385
You crazy bastard.

469
00:43:58,469 --> 00:43:59,970
What choice did I have?

470
00:44:00,554 --> 00:44:01,555
I have to live too.

471
00:44:01,639 --> 00:44:03,724
Fucking bastard.

472
00:44:15,861 --> 00:44:16,695
Noja.

473
00:44:18,947 --> 00:44:20,324
Can I stay with you?

474
00:44:22,910 --> 00:44:24,536
I've got no one but you now.

475
00:44:26,497 --> 00:44:28,165
Stop bullshitting.

476
00:44:28,666 --> 00:44:30,042
I'm not your friend.

477
00:44:30,542 --> 00:44:31,794
Not taking the money?

478
00:44:33,087 --> 00:44:34,296
What money?

479
00:44:35,631 --> 00:44:36,882
Your money.

480
00:44:37,466 --> 00:44:39,134
I can give it back to you.

481
00:44:39,218 --> 00:44:40,386
Take the money.

482
00:44:46,016 --> 00:44:47,393
That's not my money.

483
00:44:49,436 --> 00:44:52,314
I told you before, didn't I?

484
00:44:52,815 --> 00:44:54,858
No matter how shitty your life is,

485
00:44:56,568 --> 00:44:58,946
you've got to be the real one.

486
00:45:01,699 --> 00:45:03,534
Seung-gyu will come looking for you.

487
00:45:05,411 --> 00:45:09,123
That bastard's not the type
to give up on his money.

488
00:45:10,290 --> 00:45:11,792
Don't go wandering around.

489
00:45:11,875 --> 00:45:13,335
Stay hidden.

490
00:45:13,836 --> 00:45:15,212
If he catches you,

491
00:45:16,296 --> 00:45:17,881
you won't die easy.

492
00:45:26,473 --> 00:45:27,808
Where are you buying smokes?

493
00:45:30,310 --> 00:45:31,645
Over there.

494
00:45:37,818 --> 00:45:41,280
Why do you wear fake glasses? You dumbass.

495
00:45:49,079 --> 00:45:50,497
The light changed.

496
00:45:50,581 --> 00:45:51,498
Get lost.

497
00:46:51,308 --> 00:46:52,226
Just…

498
00:46:52,309 --> 00:46:53,435
Just a moment.

499
00:47:00,526 --> 00:47:04,822
THE RAT

500
00:47:21,713 --> 00:47:22,548
THE RAT
VOLUME TWO

501
00:47:24,258 --> 00:47:27,886
Volumes one and two
are usually released together.

502
00:47:28,387 --> 00:47:32,558
Since volume two wasn't finished in time,
we released volume one first.

503
00:47:33,225 --> 00:47:37,312
Readers are going crazy right now.

504
00:47:38,438 --> 00:47:41,233
Volume two needs to come out soon.
They are waiting for it.

505
00:47:43,777 --> 00:47:44,736
We

506
00:47:45,237 --> 00:47:47,489
might become really famous.

507
00:47:47,573 --> 00:47:49,533
Hurry home and finish editing it.

508
00:47:52,327 --> 00:47:54,288
Apartment 705, Luchena Tower, Gangnam.

509
00:47:55,247 --> 00:47:58,500
The passcode is 0912.
You know that, right?

510
00:49:00,062 --> 00:49:03,190
I LOATHE EVERYTHING ABOUT YOU…
THE RAT

511
00:49:04,024 --> 00:49:05,859
<i>This story is entirely true.</i>

512
00:49:07,361 --> 00:49:09,196
<i>I killed someone.</i>

513
00:49:10,155 --> 00:49:13,450
<i>This is a record of my crime</i>
<i>and a letter of confession.</i>

514
00:49:14,785 --> 00:49:17,871
<i>This is proof that I'm the Rat.</i>

515
00:49:29,216 --> 00:49:30,884
Wait, this…

516
00:49:37,724 --> 00:49:38,642
No.

517
00:49:39,434 --> 00:49:40,268
This…

518
00:49:41,061 --> 00:49:42,938
This should never get out.

519
00:49:43,021 --> 00:49:44,022
This…

520
00:49:44,648 --> 00:49:47,901
This is proof I'm the Rat, not a human.

521
00:49:49,069 --> 00:49:50,654
<i>This isn't the end.</i>

522
00:49:51,154 --> 00:49:53,448
<i>You won't be able to handle it.</i>

523
00:49:54,950 --> 00:49:57,995
DEFENDANT

524
00:49:58,078 --> 00:49:58,996
Mr. Park.

525
00:49:59,496 --> 00:50:02,082
Is there anything you'd like to add?

526
00:50:04,960 --> 00:50:06,837
PLAINTIFF

527
00:50:10,007 --> 00:50:11,675
I recently found my uncle.

528
00:50:13,176 --> 00:50:15,178
He's not related to me by blood,

529
00:50:16,346 --> 00:50:19,349
and I barely remembered him.

530
00:50:21,476 --> 00:50:23,729
But when I was little,

531
00:50:24,938 --> 00:50:26,648
he was like a father to me.

532
00:50:27,524 --> 00:50:30,277
He's already at the tail end of his life.

533
00:50:32,029 --> 00:50:33,739
Seeing him again

534
00:50:35,532 --> 00:50:39,036
made me think about

535
00:50:39,953 --> 00:50:40,787
what family means.

536
00:50:45,751 --> 00:50:46,960
I remember…

537
00:50:48,962 --> 00:50:53,050
reading the phrase
"the beginning of the end"

538
00:50:53,675 --> 00:50:55,802
somewhere a long time ago.

539
00:50:56,386 --> 00:50:57,721
The thing is,

540
00:50:58,555 --> 00:51:02,184
I'm not very smart,
so I don't know exactly what it means.

541
00:51:02,267 --> 00:51:03,810
But I thought…

542
00:51:07,272 --> 00:51:10,067
it didn't mean that the end was beginning…

543
00:51:12,694 --> 00:51:15,238
but that things begin at the end.

544
00:51:16,865 --> 00:51:20,160
That was just how I interpreted it
back then.

545
00:51:21,703 --> 00:51:25,624
I know it's because I failed
as a husband and father

546
00:51:25,707 --> 00:51:28,835
that my family has come
to the end of the road

547
00:51:30,670 --> 00:51:31,505
like this.

548
00:51:33,507 --> 00:51:34,341
But if…

549
00:51:36,635 --> 00:51:38,053
at the end of this road…

550
00:51:39,471 --> 00:51:41,473
I'm given one last chance…

551
00:51:45,102 --> 00:51:45,977
If you can…

552
00:51:48,605 --> 00:51:49,981
If I could…

553
00:51:52,901 --> 00:51:54,402
somehow get that chance,

554
00:51:54,903 --> 00:51:55,987
I…

555
00:51:58,115 --> 00:51:59,825
I'd like to start over.

556
00:51:59,908 --> 00:52:02,786
MEDIATION JUDGE

557
00:52:10,043 --> 00:52:11,002
If I were given…

558
00:52:14,548 --> 00:52:16,341
one last chance.

559
00:53:22,908 --> 00:53:23,783
Hey!

560
00:53:31,791 --> 00:53:32,626
You're here?

561
00:53:32,709 --> 00:53:34,461
It's so hot today, so…

562
00:53:34,544 --> 00:53:36,171
Don't just stand there.

563
00:53:36,254 --> 00:53:37,839
If you're here, help out.

564
00:53:37,923 --> 00:53:41,635
I need to tend to that dying one
and pick and dry the chili peppers.

565
00:53:41,718 --> 00:53:42,969
Perfect timing.

566
00:53:43,053 --> 00:53:44,429
Go change and come back.

567
00:54:46,616 --> 00:54:48,326
<i>The Rat thought</i>

568
00:54:48,952 --> 00:54:52,247
<i>that it could never escape from here.</i>

569
00:54:53,832 --> 00:54:55,166
<i>The perfect rathole.</i>

570
00:54:55,834 --> 00:54:58,628
<i>There would be no place safer than here.</i>

571
00:54:58,712 --> 00:54:59,796
<i>But…</i>

572
00:55:00,922 --> 00:55:01,923
<i>But</i>

573
00:55:03,508 --> 00:55:07,387
<i>after weeks of agonizing recollection,</i>

574
00:55:08,263 --> 00:55:11,349
<i>the Rat finally realized</i>
<i>that it was that loathsome Rat.</i>

575
00:55:13,893 --> 00:55:15,228
<i>Everything was a dream.</i>

576
00:55:16,896 --> 00:55:19,190
<i>A dream made by endless self-loathing.</i>

577
00:55:24,195 --> 00:55:27,073
<i>There wasn't a shred of truth in it.</i>

578
00:55:28,199 --> 00:55:29,409
<i>It had gone insane.</i>

579
00:55:29,909 --> 00:55:31,870
<i>Even dreams and reality…</i>

580
00:55:31,953 --> 00:55:33,872
HAN JI-HYE, EDITOR-IN-CHIEF
WE CAN'T WAIT ANYMORE!

581
00:55:33,955 --> 00:55:35,332
No!

582
00:55:35,415 --> 00:55:36,416
Fuck.

583
00:55:37,000 --> 00:55:38,585
No. Fuck.

584
00:55:38,668 --> 00:55:39,794
Just wait!

585
00:55:59,356 --> 00:56:01,399
Who is it? What kind of fucking…

586
00:56:06,029 --> 00:56:07,614
Fuck off!

587
00:56:08,615 --> 00:56:10,825
I said fuck off! You fucking bastards.

588
00:56:15,580 --> 00:56:16,498
Try and come in.

589
00:56:16,998 --> 00:56:19,167
Try and come in! You fucking bastards!

590
00:57:24,065 --> 00:57:27,026
<i>How have you been, you fucking bastard?</i>

591
00:57:30,280 --> 00:57:31,948
<i>Didn't think I'd find you, did you?</i>

592
00:57:33,199 --> 00:57:35,034
<i>Open the door, you fucking bastard.</i>

593
00:57:36,244 --> 00:57:39,581
<i>I said open the door, you fucking bastard!</i>

594
00:57:52,510 --> 00:57:54,053
<i>Hey, rat bastard.</i>

595
00:57:55,138 --> 00:57:57,223
<i>I know you're hiding in there.</i>

596
00:57:59,309 --> 00:58:01,978
<i>Hey, we've got to settle this money issue,</i>

597
00:58:03,563 --> 00:58:05,773
<i>or this is never going to end.</i>

598
00:58:07,484 --> 00:58:09,569
<i>Hey, rat bastard. Open the door now.</i>

599
00:58:10,695 --> 00:58:12,989
<i>I said open the door, you fucking bastard!</i>

600
00:58:14,908 --> 00:58:17,744
MOUSETRAP

601
01:02:42,175 --> 01:02:45,094
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
